# Power quotas (linuxcnc/powerquota): the six drives' input power over
# smart-serial (stmbl-arm.0.J.power, as hm2_*.stbl.*.power) into the
# supply's fuses ([POWERQUOTA]CONFIG), the feed scale into adaptive feed
# (M52 P1), an alarm into the estop chain. A HALFILE right after
# arcmate.hal: it goes into the chain after the collision guard and drives
# estop-chain itself, which grip.hal / changer.hal then take on from.
loadrt powerquota config=[POWERQUOTA]CONFIG
addf powerquota.0 servo-thread

net j0-power stmbl-arm.0.0.power => powerquota.0.power-0
net j1-power stmbl-arm.0.1.power => powerquota.0.power-1
net j2-power stmbl-arm.0.2.power => powerquota.0.power-2
net j3-power stmbl-arm.0.3.power => powerquota.0.power-3
net j4-power stmbl-arm.0.4.power => powerquota.0.power-4
net j5-power stmbl-arm.0.5.power => powerquota.0.power-5
net feed-scale powerquota.0.feed-scale => motion.adaptive-feed

# into the estop chain: estop-and (the GUI's enable, no collision) ->
# powerquota -> estop-chain (-> iocontrol, or the gripper's / changer's)
unlinkp estop-and.out
net estop-guard estop-and.out => powerquota.0.chain-in
net estop-chain powerquota.0.chain-out
net estop-reset => powerquota.0.reset
